no production WSGI server, the SQLite thread-safety fix untested under a
real multi-worker server, and no documented resolution for the
two-Python-environment split at deploy time.

requirements.txt (runtime) / requirements-dev.txt (adds pytest tooling)
generated from `pip freeze` against the global interpreter, hand-checked
against actual imports across src/, tools/, and tests/ (excluding
tests/voice/). decisions/0014-deploy-target-and-voice-scope.md records
four explicit decisions: voice/AI4Bharat excluded from the deployed
instance (demoed locally — ~6.8GB of weights + torch doesn't fit
Render's free-tier 512MB); gunicorn==26.2.0 as the production WSGI
server, verified for real via a throwaway WSL environment (gunicorn
